{{Quote|An Aqualish merchant? Shouldn't you be roughing up some Bith for credits?''"<br />"''Not all Aqualish are like that; besides, Bith are hard to come by.|[[Meetra Surik]] and [[Margar]] address Aqualish stereotypes in the galaxy|<ref name="Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II: The Sith Lords">''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II: The Sith Lords]]''</ref>}}
The '''Aqualish''' were tusked [[Humanoid/Legends|humanoids]] from the [[Planet/Legends|planet]] [[Ando/Legends|Ando]] whose appearance combined aspects of arachnids and pinniped aquatic mammals. Aqualish had a reputation for being nasty, crude and aggressive, and generally pursued off-world careers as [[Mercenary/Legends|mercenaries]], [[Bounty hunter/Legends|bounty hunters]], and [[Pirate/Legends|pirates]]. One of the most infamous such Aqualish was the [[Smuggler/Legends|smuggler]] [[Ponda Baba/Legends|Ponda Baba]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Aqualish2.jpg|thumb|left|180px|A male Quara (left) and a female Aquala (right).]]
An [[Amphibian/Legends|amphibious]] species native to the planet [[Ando/Legends|Ando]], the Aqualish people were made up of three distinct races which included the '''Aquala''', the '''Ualaq''' and the '''Quara'''. Although they all had their differences, their baseline genetic structure was the same and their appearances did not vary so drastically as to characterize them as different species. All Aqualish had two facial tusks which curved down over their mouths; a trait which added to their appearance as [[Spider/Legends|arachnids]].<ref name="UAA" /> Indeed, the Aqualish had some arachnid genetic material in their distant past, as demonstrative in their relationship with the [[Harch/Legends|Harch species]].<ref name="TEGTW">''[[The Essential Guide to Warfare]]''</ref> These facial tusks were highly sensitive to heat and cold and were used for cracking open the hard shells of shellfish or burrowing through the swampy loam of their homeworld.<ref name="NEGAS" />

These species are well known for their hair-trigger tempers that flare without reason.<ref name="NEGAS" /> Anthropologists believe that the streak of rage can be dated back to the species' earliest evolutions.<ref name="NEGAS" />

The [[Aquala/Legends|Aquala]] subspecies was considered to be the baseline Aqualish breed. Having finned hands and two bulbous black [[Eye/Legends|eyes]], the Aquala were unable to manipulate most machinery or equipment developed by the galaxy's many species which designed these tools for beings with digits. As a result, Aquala tended to remain on their homeworld in greater numbers than either of the other subspecies.<ref name="UAA" /> The Aquala hated their [[Quara/Legends|Quara]] relatives, which was characteristic of each of the subspecies sharing a hatred of each other as they believed their race to be the most superior. The Quara had developed clawed, five-fingered hands and like the Aquala had two eyes. Combined with the Ualaq, the Quara made up only ten percent of the Aqualish population. This was due to their ability to use equipment off-world designed for fingered species; Thus, they were the subspecies more commonly found off-world.<ref name="UAA" /> The [[Ualaq/Legends|Ualaq]], considered by some specialists to be the result of genetic mutation,<ref name="Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> had four eyes instead of two and fingered hands which varied from three to five digits on each.<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> The least common subspecies, the Ualaq often times journeyed far from Ando to avoid discrimination by the Aquala.<ref name="UAA" />

==Society and culture==
The Aquala hated their [[Quara/Legends|Quara]] relatives, as they blamed them for the image the Aqualish had in the galaxy as thugs. Because of this, the latter subspecies were considered pariahs on Ando, which had a lower population of Aqualish than the galaxy itself.<ref name="Doctor Death: The Tale of Dr. Evazan and Ponda Baba">{{StoryCite|story=Doctor Death: The Tale of Dr. Evazan and Ponda Baba|book=Tales from the Mos Eisley Cantina}}</ref> All three Aqualish subspecies spoke mutually intelligible dialects of the same [[Aqualish (language)/Legends|language]]. Quarrelsome and thug-like, the Aqualish culture revolved around aggression and toughness, with diplomacy being one of their weakest attributes.<ref name="NEGAS" />

[[File:PoNudoEpII-SWCTP.png|thumb|right|Po Nudo, the Ualaq Senator who led his people in seceding from the Republic during the Clone Wars.]]

==History==
The Aqualish evolved into three races which were constantly at war with each other: the Aquala, the baseline race of the oceans, the Quara of the wetlands, and the Ualaq of the caves and dark rain forests. Each race believed they were the dominant branch, and allegations leveled by the Aquala that the other two races caused a decline in the harvests of fish eventually escalated into the [[Aqualish Civil War]]. In a shocking turn of events, the war ultimately ended in a treaty which saw the unification of all three races. After the war ended, a group of [[Human/Legends|Human]] settlers stumbled upon the world and were killed by the startled and aggressive Aqualish. Confiscating the ship which brought the supposed invaders to the world, the Aqualish extrapolated the secrets of [[Realspace/Legends|space]] travel from the exploratory craft and set forth on a campaign of conquest to the neighboring world of [[Andando]]. Not long after the landing, Andando was left a smoldering ruin, rendered inhospitable by the barbarous Aqualish.<ref name="wizards">{{Wizards|url=default.asp?x=starwars/article/sw20030703ando|text=Ando: Planet of the Walrus Men|int=Ando: Planet of the Walrus Men}}</ref>

Discovered by the [[Galactic Republic/Legends|Galactic Republic]] during the [[Great Manifest Period/Legends|Great Manifest Period]], envoys attempted to make contact with the inhabitants of Ando and were rebuked with hostile fire. This quickly led to the [[Aqualish–Republic War]] that, while bloody, quickly ended in the defeat of the Aqualish. Defeated, Ando joined the Republic in [[15,000 BBY/Legends|15,000 BBY]] and began an era of colonization which resulted in the formation of the [[Andoan Free Colonies/Legends|Andoan Free Colonies]]<ref name="HNN49">{{HoloNetNewsWeb|49|regional/13328_1.html|Andoan Free Colonies Criticize Aqualish}}</ref>; an event concurrent with the [[Ando separation]].<ref name="Hnn-Quick Poll">{{HoloNetNewsWeb|47||Quick Poll}}</ref> Due to the constant violence erupting across the world, however, the Republic dispatched the [[Ando Demilitarization Observation Group]] to ensure the de-escalation of violence; [[Jedi Master/Legends|Master]] [[Jorus C'baoth]] of the [[Jedi Order/Legends|Jedi Order]] served as one of the group's primary observers.<ref name="wizards" />

[[File:Pirate_TotG.jpg|thumb|left|200px|An Aqualish pirate]]
Represented in the [[Galactic Senate/Legends|Galactic Senate]] by [[Po Nudo/Legends|Po Nudo]] before the [[Separatist Crisis/Legends|Separatist Crisis]], the world seceded in [[23 BBY/Legends|23 BBY]] along with [[Sy Myrth/Legends|Sy Myrth]], a move contested by the Andoan Free Colonies, which retained representation in the Senate under [[Gorothin Vagger]].<ref name="HNN49" /> Nudo became a prominent Separatist leader and a member of the [[Separatist Council/Legends|Separatist Council]]. As the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]] spread across the galaxy, a [[Battle of Ando|civil war]] broke out between both Nudo and Vagger's factions of Aqualish. Despite assistance from the [[Grand Army of the Republic/Legends|Grand Army of the Republic]] and Jedi Master [[Shaak Ti/Legends|Shaak Ti]], the battle ended in a Separatist victory.<ref name="Republic HoloNet News Core Edition 14:3:22">{{InsiderCite|66|Republic HoloNet News Core Edition 14:3:22}}</ref> When the [[Galactic Empire/Legends|Galactic Empire]] rose to power at the end of the war, former Separatist worlds suffered heavily from intense Imperial scrutiny. Appointing an Aquala Senator to replace the recently murdered Nudo, the Senator served until the disbanding of the [[Imperial Senate/Legends|Imperial Senate]] in [[0 BBY/Legends|0 BBY]]. Establishing an Imperial garrison on Ando, the Imperials ravaged the world's natural resources, using them to further the Empire's war machine. Following the death of [[Emperor/Legends|Emperor]] [[Palpatine/Legends|Palpatine]], Ando joined the [[New Republic/Legends|New Republic]] only to fall into the sight of one of [[Grand Admiral/Legends|Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo/Legends|Mitth'raw'nuruodo's]] [[Battle of Ando (Thrawn campaign)|feint attacks]] in preparation for his attack on [[Ukio/Legends|Ukio]]. Sending the [[Bellicose (Imperial-class)/Legends|''Bellicose'']] in [[9 ABY/Legends|9 ABY]], the world was taken by [[Thrawn's confederation]].<ref name="TEA">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

During the [[Yuuzhan Vong War]], Ando was [[Invasion of Ando (Yuuzhan Vong War)|attacked]] by the [[Yuuzhan Vong|invaders]] but was issued an ultimatum: surrender a member of the [[New Jedi Order|Jedi Order]] and destroy all droids on the planet and the Yuuzhan Vong would leave in peace. The Aqualish quickly turned on visiting [[Jedi Knight/Legends|Jedi Knight]] [[Dorsk 82]], but this was ignored by [[Warmaster]] [[Tsavong Lah]] and an invasion and occupation of their planet ensued, enslaving the race to the foreign invaders. After the war's end, the Yuuzhan Vong abandoned the planet, thus freeing the Aqualish from occupation.<ref name="The New Jedi Order: Edge of Victory I: Conquest">''[[The New Jedi Order: Edge of Victory I: Conquest]]''</ref> Ando remained independent and disunited, and therefore never joined the [[Galactic Federation of Free Alliances|Galactic Alliance]]. As of [[137 ABY]], Ando was a member of [[Darth Krayt]]'s [[Darth Krayt's Galactic Empire|Galactic Empire]].<ref name="TEA" />

===Aqualish in the galaxy===
[[File:Swindled_TCG_Core_set.jpg|thumb|right|250px|An [[Unidentified Aqualish bounty hunter (Outer Rim)|Aqualish bounty hunter]] with two [[Twi'lek/Legends|Twi'leks]].]]
While originally confined to their homeworld, contact with the Galactic Republic opened up space transit for the Aqualish and the colonization of the [[Andoan Free Colonies/Legends|Andoan Free Colonies]].
A community of [[Whiphid/Legends|Whiphids]] and Aqualish lived on the planet [[Gertafuu VI]], trading with exotic foodstuff and furs.<ref name="Bartyn's Landing article">{{GamerCite|7|Bartyn's Landing (article)}}</ref>

There were also a number of Aqualish in [[Bartyn's Landing]], the capital town of [[Lamaredd/Legends|Lamaredd]], c. [[29 BBY]].<ref name="G7R">{{GamerCite|7|Reckonings}}</ref>

While [[Force-sensitive/Legends|Forceful]] Aqualish were quite rare, members of the species did go on to train in both the [[Jedi Order/Legends|Jedi Order]] and the [[Sith Empire/Legends|Sith Empire]]. During the [[Jedi Civil War]], an [[Unidentified Aqualish Sith hopeful|Aqualish acolyte]] attempted to become initiated in the ways of the [[Sith/Legends|Sith]] on [[Korriban/Legends|Korriban]] but was ultimately dissuaded by [[Jedi Master/Legends|Jedi Master]] [[Revan/Legends|Revan]].<ref name="Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic">''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic]]''</ref> Millennium later, two Quara were trained as Jedi; both [[Windo Nend]]<ref name="BoJ">''[[Star Wars: Republic: The Battle of Jabiim]]''</ref> and an [[Unidentified Aqualish Jedi|able Jedi pilot]] were killed during the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]].<ref name="The Clone Wars 11">[[The Clone Wars 11|''The Clone Wars'' 11]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In one of ''A New Hope''{{'s}} best-known continuity errors, Ponda Baba's arm has fin-like hands when still attached, but is hairy and clawed in the close-up shots of the severed arm on the floor. This inspired the writers at [[West End Games]] to develop the Aquala and Quara types of Aqualish. ''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary]]'' [[Retroactive continuity|retconned]] the error by creating a new character, [[Teak Sidbam/Legends|Teak Sidbam]], said to be sometimes mistaken for Baba.

When Aqualish characters appeared in the [[prequel trilogy]], more detailed, four-eyed masks&mdash;Ualaq masks&mdash;were used.

In the game files (Kotor Tool) of ''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic]]'', the Quara Aqualish are referred to as "walrusmen".

